rom 9 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The Netherlands were the defending gold medalists and were favored again, having won the 2023 World Championships and the Luzern Regatta. Their biggest rivals were thought to be Poland, the 2022 World Champion and bronze medalist at the 2023 Worlds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Netherlands defended their gold medal with relative ease, leading at every checkpoint, although Italy closed strongly to take the silver medal, after trailing Poland at 1,500 metres. Poland held on for the bronze medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This was the Netherlands first gold medal at Paris 2024, but it gave them 150 golds, Summer and Winter combined. " [:a {:href "/athletes/135281"} "Tone Wieten"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/145583"} "Koen Metsemakers"] " were part of both winning Dutch crews in 2020 and 2024. For Wieten, this was his third Olympic medal, also winning a bronze medal in the 2016 eight. All members of the Italian and Polish crews had competed previously at the Olympics but all of them won their first Olympic medals in Paris."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Italy’s silver medal was its first medal in the event since 2008, although it was their fifth medal overall in this event, tying them with Great Britain for most medals in men’s quad sculls. Poland’s bronze medal was its second medal in the event, after they had won gold in 2008."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Netherlands"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/153788"} "Lennart van Lierop"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/145579"} "Finn Florijn"] " 